My first ascension. It was actually pretty easy. I found a wand of
wishing (0:3) on level 3. More on that in a sec.

I started with +o detect monsters, =o invisibility, =o +1const, and a /
o locking.

I wished for 2b?oCharging, SDSM, speed boots, helm of brilliance,
gauntlets of dexterity and an amulet of life saving. It was a good
thing I wished for the amulet, because I got crushed to death by a
bugbear/owlbear shortly after. So, I wished for another one, just in
case.

The biggest difficulty I had was that I was not finding any ?oID and
couldn't get Thoth to give me Magicbane. A while later I learned
create monster and got Magicbane (and stealth, speed, fire brand and
giantslayer). I also wished for a magic marker and wrote +oID and
+oPoly. I like knowing the spell of identify. It makes things much
more straightforward for me. I didn't really get anything useful from
polypiling. I was hoping a unihorn would turn into a marker, but no
dice. I didn't know magic missile, either, so I was using a crysknife
for a long time.

I genocided master mind flayers from a throne and L. I meant to write
a cursed ?oGenocide but did it with a blessed marker (oops) so I did R
too. I got a wish from a throne but must have misspelled "magic
marker" because I got a +o Detect Unseen (yay!).

I progressed pretty easily through the quest, bought protection with
the profits from Ludios, and was all set for Gehennom. Except I was
only level 19 and had ~180 HP. So I walked around for a while,
consorted with succubi, reverse genocided nurses (once, getting about
50 HP, I was impressed) and wraiths (twice, getting 4 or 5 levels; two
of the corpses were rotten -- lame). Then I went down to hell.

I knew magic mapping and had plenty of wands of digging. Gehennom was
pretty easy. The Wizard died to finger of death on the first shot. The
mysterious force sent me back a couple of times, but nothing bad. I
met an Archon on level 3 who summoned nasties a lot. I was surrounded
for quite a while but was eventually able to run away.

Earth was easy, air was harder but I took refuge in a fog cloud. Fire
was easy and so was water. Astral took a while but the left altar had
famine and belonged to Thoth. Done.

Looking at the end-of-game output, I only killed the Wizard 3x. He is
guaranteed when you get the book from him and guaranteed when you go
to the plane of earth, right? So I only saw him once more than the
minimum. I don't think the RNG could have been a lot nicer to me.

